    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts",
      "apiVersion": "2025-06-01",
      "name": "[variables('name')]",
      "location": "[resourceGroup().location]",
      "sku": { "name": "[parameters('storageSku')]" },
      "kind": "StorageV2"
    }
  ]
}
```

A deployment supplies `prefix` as `ab` and `storageSku` as `Basic_LRS`. What happens?

A team is comparing an ARM JSON dependency with a Bicep dependency.

```json
{
  "type": "Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces",
  "apiVersion": "2025-01-01",
  "name": "nic-app1",
  "location": "[resourceGroup().location]",
  "dependsOn": [
    "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/publicIPAddresses', 'pip-app1')]"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "ipConfigurations": [
      {
        "name": "ipconfig1",
        "properties": {
          "privateIPAllocationMethod": "Dynamic",
          "publicIPAddress": {
            "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/publicIPAddresses', 'pip-app1')]"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```bicep
param location string = resourceGroup().location

resource pip 'Microsoft.Network/publicIPAddresses@2025-01-01' = {
  name: 'pip-app1'
  location: location
  sku: {
    name: 'Basic'
  }
  properties: {
    publicIPAllocationMethod: 'Dynamic'
  }
}

resource nic 'Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces@2025-01-01' = {
  name: 'nic-app1'
  location: location
  properties: {
    ipConfigurations: [
      {
        name: 'ipconfig1'
        properties: {
          privateIPAllocationMethod: 'Dynamic'
          publicIPAddress: {
            id: pip.id
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Which two statements are correct? Each correct answer presents part of the solution. Select TWO.

